## ISS-013: Non-atomic analytics data flush risks file corruption

### File
`/root/Redball/src/Redball.UI.WPF/Services/AnalyticsService.cs`

### Original
```csharp
            _lock.EnterReadLock();
            var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = true };
            var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(_data, options);
            File.WriteAllText(AnalyticsFile, json);
            Logger.Debug("Analytics", "Analytics data flushed to disk");
```

### Replacement
```csharp
            _lock.EnterReadLock();
            var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { WriteIndented = true };
            var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(_data, options);
            var tempFile = AnalyticsFile + ".tmp";
            File.WriteAllText(tempFile, json);
            File.Move(tempFile, AnalyticsFile, overwrite: true);
            Logger.Debug("Analytics", "Analytics data flushed to disk");
```

### Reason
Writes to a temporary file and then atomically replaces the target, preventing a half-written file if the process is killed.

### Verification
`dotnet build ...` and unit test.
